# Paired Dual-Craft Route: Enchanting + Tailoring 1-300 (WoW: Forever)
# Follows docs/MULTI_PROFESSION_RULES.md:
# - Dedicated per-combination file: guides/pairs/enchanting-tailoring.guide
# - Dual-Craft pair: Tailoring is the Producer (its crafted greens and the
#   cloth-band loot feed Enchanting disenchanting), so every `section` header
#   is Tailoring in rising order. Enchanting steps (train / learn / craft /
#   buy / auction / collect) are interleaved inside the Tailoring brackets
#   and there is never a `section Enchanting` header, so lint and the
#   Materials tracker see one anchor profession.
# - Every `collect ... gather` has a matching `auction` goal in the same
#   section so Mix / Gather / Buy modes all work.
# - Tailoring steps, ids and counts follow guides/tailoring.guide; Enchanting
#   steps, ids and counts follow guides/enchanting.guide (Strange Dust tab).
#   All NPC, item, spell and quest ids are copied from those two verified
#   solo guides (Forever client tables, build 1.60.1).
# - Disenchant is not a spellbook spell in Forever (it ships with Apprentice
#   Enchanting and lives in the Enchanting box of the Professions window), so
#   disenchanting is taught in tips and not as a learn step.
# - The Forever dye recipes (Cerulean, Magenta, Viridian) are Alchemy
#   products; this pair has no Herbalism or Alchemy, so the tips point you
#   at the Auction House for them. The recipes on this route use the vendor
#   Red Dye, not the Alchemy dyes.

guide forever-professions/pair-enchanting-tailoring
title Enchanting + Tailoring 1-300
category Professions
folder Paired Routes
coords era
levels 1-60
zone Azeroth
keywords enchanting, tailoring, paired, cloth, disenchant, dyes

pitch Level Tailoring and Enchanting together from 1 to 300: turn your own cloth into gear, then turn the gear into enchanting dust.
pro Two crafting professions means 6 Legacy Points (3 each at skill 150, 225 and 300) from a single character
pro No gathering profession needed: cloth drops from humanoids while you level, and crafted and looted greens become Enchanting dust and essence
con Forever's Alchemy dyes (Cerulean, Magenta, Viridian) must come from the Auction House unless you have an Alchemy alt
con Both professions eat gold early; Strange Dust, rods and 2000-odd Runecloth are the bulk of the shopping list

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice

section Tailoring 1-55

step Learn Tailoring
  only Alliance
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Tailoring and Enchanting take both primary slots, and neither needs a gatherer: cloth drops from humanoids. Lawrence Schneider in Stormwind teaches Apprentice Tailoring, at any character level. The starting trainer in Elwynn (Eldrin Eastvale, Eastvale Logging Camp) teaches it too; Dwarves, Gnomes and Night Elves come to the capital. Buy Coarse Thread from the Tailoring Supply vendor nearby.
  train Tailoring Apprentice npc 1300

step Learn Tailoring
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Tailoring and Enchanting take both primary slots, and neither needs a gatherer: cloth drops from humanoids. Snang in Orgrimmar teaches Apprentice Tailoring, at any character level. The starting trainer in Tirisfal (Bowen Brisboise, Cold Hearth Manor, south-west of Brill) teaches it too; Orcs, Trolls and Tauren come to the capital. Buy Coarse Thread from the Tailoring Supply vendor nearby; the Tirisfal trainer has none, so buy it in Brill from Abigail Shiel.
  train Tailoring Apprentice npc 2855

step Learn Enchanting
  only Alliance
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Lucan Cordell in Stormwind teaches Apprentice Enchanting, at any character level, and Journeyman too, so you return to the same trainer. Disenchant comes with Apprentice Enchanting: in Forever it is in the Enchanting box of the Professions window, not the spellbook. From now on, never vendor a green (uncommon) weapon or armor piece: disenchant it instead. Mote of Magic comes only from Enchanting Supply vendors.
  train Enchanting Apprentice npc 1317

step Learn Enchanting
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Jhag in Orgrimmar teaches Apprentice Enchanting, at any character level. (The Durotar starting trainer is Pa'zula in Sen'jin Village.) Disenchant comes with Apprentice Enchanting: in Forever it is in the Enchanting box of the Professions window, not the spellbook. From now on, never vendor a green (uncommon) weapon or armor piece: disenchant it instead. Mote of Magic comes only from Enchanting Supply vendors.
  train Enchanting Apprentice npc 11066

step Tailoring 1-55: vendor goods
  tip Coarse Thread for the Linen Belts: 28, from any Tailoring Supply vendor.
  buy 2320 x28 nearest

step Enchanting 1-70: vendor goods
  tip Mote of Magic (19) and a Copper Rod (1), both from the Enchanting Supply vendor near the Enchanting trainer, not the Auction House.
  buy 247786 x19 nearest
  buy 6217 x1 nearest

step Tailoring 1-55: Auction House
  tip What 1-55 takes that the Auction House sells: 60 Linen Cloth for the Tailoring bolts and 50 Strange Dust for the Enchanting stretch. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 2589 x60
  auction 10940 x50

step Linen Cloth
  tip Linen Cloth drops from humanoids of level 5-20: keep what you loot as you level, or take it from your bank.
  collect 2589 x60 anywhere gather levels 5-20

step Strange Dust
  tip Strange Dust comes from disenchanting green items of item level 1-20. Disenchant the early greens you loot or win in quests, or take dust from your bank.
  collect 10940 x50 anywhere gather Enchanting 1

step Bolt of Linen Cloth (1-30)
  tip Bolt of Linen Cloth, 30 bolts to about 30: 2 Linen Cloth each. Keep every bolt: the Linen Belts take 28 of them.
  learn 2963 "Bolt of Linen Cloth"
  craft 2963 "Bolt of Linen Cloth" x30

step Linen Belt (30-55)
  tip Linen Belt, 28 belts to 55: 1 Bolt of Linen Cloth and 1 Coarse Thread each. Vendor the belts: whites give no dust.
  learn 8776 "Linen Belt"
  craft 8776 "Linen Belt" until 55

step Runed Copper Rod (Enchanting 1-2)
  tip Runed Copper Rod, 1 craft to Enchanting 2: 1 Copper Rod and 1 Mote of Magic. Keep it in your bags: every enchant to 110 needs a runed rod in hand, and the Copper one is it until the Silver Rod at 109.
  learn 7421 "Runed Copper Rod"
  craft 7421 "Runed Copper Rod" x1

step Enchant Bracer - Inferior Stamina (Enchanting 2-20)
  tip Enchant Bracer - Inferior Stamina, 18 to Enchanting 20: 1 Mote of Magic each. Enchant any bracers in your bags, even grey ones.
  learn 7418 "Enchant Bracer - Inferior Stamina"
  craft 7418 "Enchant Bracer - Inferior Stamina" until 20

step Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina (Enchanting 20-70)
  tip Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina, 50 to Enchanting 70: 1 Strange Dust each. Apprentice Enchanting caps at 75, so stop here until you have Journeyman.
  learn 7420 "Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina"
  craft 7420 "Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina" until 70

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Journeyman

section Tailoring 55-125

step Journeyman Tailoring
  only Alliance
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Journeyman Tailoring raises the cap to 150; it needs skill 50 and level 10. Sellandus in Stormwind teaches it (Jormund Stonebrow in Ironforge and Me'lynn in Darnassus do too). Learn it before the Woolen Bolts: points stop at 75 without it.
  level 10
  train Tailoring Journeyman npc 5567

step Journeyman Tailoring
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Journeyman Tailoring raises the cap to 150; it needs skill 50 and level 10. Magar in Orgrimmar teaches it (Rhiannon Davis in Undercity and Tepa in Thunder Bluff do too). Learn it before the Woolen Bolts: points stop at 75 without it.
  level 10
  train Tailoring Journeyman npc 3363

step Journeyman Enchanting
  only Alliance
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Journeyman Enchanting raises the cap to 150; it needs skill 50 and level 10. Lucan Cordell in Stormwind teaches it, while you are already in the capital for Tailoring (Gimble Thistlefuzz in Ironforge and Taladan in Darnassus do too).
  level 10
  train Enchanting Journeyman npc 1317

step Journeyman Enchanting
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Journeyman Enchanting raises the cap to 150; it needs skill 50 and level 10. Godan in Orgrimmar teaches it (Lavinia Crowe in Undercity and Teg Dawnstrider in Thunder Bluff do too). Note the change of trainer: Jhag, who taught Apprentice, does not teach Journeyman.
  level 10
  train Enchanting Journeyman npc 3345

step Tailoring 55-125: vendor goods
  tip Fine Thread for the capes, shoulders and gloves: 47, from any Tailoring Supply vendor.
  buy 2321 x47 nearest

step Tailoring 55-125: Auction House
  tip What 55-125 takes that the Auction House sells: 171 Wool Cloth, 772 Silk Cloth and 5 Elixir of Wisdom (an Alchemy product) for Tailoring; 120 Strange Dust, 4 Lesser Magic Essence, 1 Shadowgem and 1 Silver Rod for Enchanting. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold. Forever's Alchemy dye patterns (Cerulean, Magenta, Viridian Dye) are not needed on this route; if you want them later, buy them here too.
  auction 2592 x171
  auction 4306 x772
  auction 3383 x5
  auction 10940 x120
  auction 10938 x4
  auction 1210 x1
  auction 6338 x1

step Wool Cloth
  tip Wool Cloth drops from humanoids of level 15-30: keep what you loot as you level, or take it from your bank.
  collect 2592 x171 anywhere gather levels 15-30

step Silk Cloth
  tip Silk Cloth drops from humanoids of level 25-45: keep what you loot as you level, or take it from your bank.
  collect 4306 x772 anywhere gather levels 25-45

step Strange Dust and Lesser Magic Essence
  tip Disenchant every green of item level 1-20 you loot, and the Double-stitched Woolen Shoulders and Gloves of Meditation you craft below if they come out green rather than white. Strange Dust and Lesser Magic Essence come from low-level greens; the Shadowgem and Silver Rod are bought, not gathered.
  collect 10940 x120 anywhere gather Enchanting 1
  collect 10938 x4 anywhere gather Enchanting 1

step Bolt of Woolen Cloth (55-80)
  tip Bolt of Woolen Cloth, 57 bolts: 3 Wool Cloth each. About 45 of them take you to 80; make all 57 now, the capes, shoulders and gloves take the rest. Keep every bolt.
  learn 2964 "Bolt of Woolen Cloth" npc 5567 only Alliance
  learn 2964 "Bolt of Woolen Cloth" npc 3363 only Horde
  craft 2964 "Bolt of Woolen Cloth" x57

step Woolen Cape (80-95)
  tip Woolen Cape, 22 capes to 95: 1 Bolt of Woolen Cloth and 1 Fine Thread each. If the bolts already took you past 80, just make capes until 95. Capes can be enchanted too: put a Minor Protection or other cloak enchant on the first one to see what the Enchanting skill buys you.
  learn 2402 "Woolen Cape"
  craft 2402 "Woolen Cape" until 95

step Double-stitched Woolen Shoulders (95-100)
  tip Double-stitched Woolen Shoulders, 5 to 100: 3 Bolt of Woolen Cloth and 2 Fine Thread each. If they come out green, disenchant them for Strange Dust; if white, vendor them.
  learn 3848 "Double-stitched Woolen Shoulders"
  craft 3848 "Double-stitched Woolen Shoulders" until 100

step Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina (Enchanting 70-85)
  tip Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina, 15 more to Enchanting 85: 1 Strange Dust each. You need Journeyman Enchanting for points beyond 75.
  craft 7420 "Enchant Chest - Inferior Stamina" until 85

step Enchant Bracer - Minor Stamina (Enchanting 85-100)
  tip Enchant Bracer - Minor Stamina, 15 to Enchanting 100: 2 Strange Dust each.
  learn 7457 "Enchant Bracer - Minor Stamina"
  craft 7457 "Enchant Bracer - Minor Stamina" until 100

step Bolt of Silk Cloth (100-120)
  tip Bolt of Silk Cloth, 193 bolts: 4 Silk Cloth each. About 54 of them take you to 120; make all 193 now, the packs, vests and pantaloons take the rest. Keep every bolt.
  learn 3839 "Bolt of Silk Cloth"
  craft 3839 "Bolt of Silk Cloth" x193

step Gloves of Meditation (120-125)
  tip Gloves of Meditation, 5 to 125: 4 Bolt of Woolen Cloth, 3 Fine Thread and 1 Elixir of Wisdom each. The elixirs are the Alchemy ones. Disenchant the gloves for dust and essence if they come out green.
  learn 3852 "Gloves of Meditation"
  craft 3852 "Gloves of Meditation" until 125

step Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection (Enchanting 100-109)
  tip Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection, 9 to Enchanting 109: 2 Strange Dust each. The formula (Formula: Imbue Cloak - Protection) is a world drop: buy it on the Auction House. Your Woolen Capes from above are good targets if you kept any.
  learn 7771 "Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection"
  craft 7771 "Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection" until 109

step Runed Silver Rod (Enchanting 109-110)
  tip Runed Silver Rod, 1 craft to Enchanting 110: 1 Silver Rod, 3 Strange Dust, 4 Lesser Magic Essence and 1 Shadowgem. The Silver Rod and every later rod are made by Blacksmiths: buy them on the Auction House. Keep the runed rod in your bags: the recipes from 130 need it.
  learn 7795 "Runed Silver Rod"
  craft 7795 "Runed Silver Rod" x1

step Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection (Enchanting 110-125)
  tip Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection again, to Enchanting 125 so Expert Enchanting unlocks alongside Expert Tailoring: 2 Strange Dust each. Yellow the whole way.
  craft 7771 "Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection" until 125

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Expert

section Tailoring 125-150

step Expert Tailoring
  only Alliance
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Expert Tailoring raises the cap to 225; it needs skill 125 and level 20. Georgio Bolero in Stormwind teaches it. Train it now: only the Expert trainers teach Bolt of Mageweave.
  level 20
  train Tailoring Expert npc 1346

step Expert Tailoring
  only Horde
  zone Undercity
  tip Expert Tailoring raises the cap to 225; it needs skill 125 and level 20. Josef Gregorian in Undercity teaches it. Train it now: only the Expert trainers teach Bolt of Mageweave.
  level 20
  train Tailoring Expert npc 4576

step Expert Enchanting
  only Alliance
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip Expert Enchanting raises the cap to 225; it needs Enchanting 125 and level 20, and costs 50 silver. Kitta Firewind, at the top of the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest, is the only Alliance Expert trainer. Elwynn is a short walk from Stormwind, so do it on the way back from the Expert Tailoring trainer.
  level 20
  train Enchanting Expert npc 11072

step Expert Enchanting
  only Horde
  zone Stonetalon Mountains
  tip Expert Enchanting raises the cap to 225; it needs Enchanting 125 and level 20, and costs 50 silver. Hgarth, up on the hill above Sun Rock Retreat in Stonetalon Mountains, is the only Horde Expert trainer.
  level 20
  train Enchanting Expert npc 11074

step Tailoring 125-150: vendor goods
  tip Fine Thread for the Small Silk Packs: 45, from any Tailoring Supply vendor.
  buy 2321 x45 nearest

step Tailoring 125-150: Auction House
  tip What 125-150 takes that the Auction House sells: 30 Heavy Leather and 635 Mageweave Cloth for Tailoring. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold. The Enchanting cloaks and boots below need 90 Strange Dust: buy it or disenchant low-level greens.
  auction 4234 x30
  auction 4338 x635
  auction 10940 x90

step Heavy Leather
  tip Heavy Leather comes from skinning beasts of level 28-40, or take it from your bank.
  collect 4234 x30 anywhere gather Skinning 140

step Mageweave Cloth
  tip Mageweave Cloth drops from humanoids of level 35-50: keep what you loot as you level, or take it from your bank.
  collect 4338 x635 anywhere gather levels 35-50

step Strange Dust for Boots
  tip Strange Dust from disenchanting greens of item level 1-20, or from your bank.
  collect 10940 x90 anywhere gather Enchanting 1

step Small Silk Pack (125-140)
  tip Small Silk Pack, 15 packs to 140: 3 Bolt of Silk Cloth, 2 Heavy Leather and 3 Fine Thread each. Bags are not disenchantable: sell or keep them.
  learn 3813 "Small Silk Pack"
  craft 3813 "Small Silk Pack" until 140

step Bolt of Mageweave (140-150)
  tip Bolt of Mageweave, 127 bolts: 5 Mageweave Cloth each. About 23 of them take you to 150; make all 127 now, the leggings, shoulders and bags take the rest. Keep every bolt. Note: the page this route follows says 144 bolts, counting 5 a bag for the Red Mageweave Bags, but the game's own tables say the bag takes 4, so 127 is the right count.
  learn 3865 "Bolt of Mageweave" npc 1346 only Alliance
  learn 3865 "Bolt of Mageweave" npc 4576 only Horde
  craft 3865 "Bolt of Mageweave" x127

step Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection (Enchanting 125-130)
  tip Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection, a few more to Enchanting 130: 2 Strange Dust each. If you come up short of 130, start the boots from the next step.
  craft 7771 "Enchant Cloak - Minor Protection" until 130

step Enchant Boots - Minor Stamina (Enchanting 130-150)
  tip Enchant Boots - Minor Stamina, 20 to Enchanting 150: 4 Strange Dust each. The formula is a world drop: buy it on the Auction House. Enchanting 150 gives your first 3 Legacy Points from this profession, alongside Tailoring 150 in the next band.
  learn 7863 "Enchant Boots - Minor Stamina"
  craft 7863 "Enchant Boots - Minor Stamina" until 150

section Tailoring 150-200

step Formula: Minor Mana Oil
  tip Formula: Minor Mana Oil, for the Enchanting stretch in this band. Sold by Kithas (Orgrimmar), Nata Dawnstrider (Thunder Bluff), Thaddeus Webb (Undercity), Vaean (Darnassus), Tilli Thistlefuzz (Ironforge) and Jessara Cordell (Stormwind) for 30 silver.
  buy 20752 x1 nearest

step Formula: Lesser Wizard Oil
  tip Formula: Lesser Wizard Oil, needed at Enchanting 200. Same six vendors as the Minor Mana Oil formula, 40 silver.
  buy 20753 x1 nearest

step Tailoring 150-200: vendor goods
  tip Red Dye (74), Fine Thread (40) and Silken Thread (100) for the vests, pantaloons and leggings, from any Tailoring Supply vendor. Maple Seed (32) from Reagent vendors and Leaded Vial (41) from Alchemy Supply vendors go to the Minor Mana Oil.
  buy 2604 x74 nearest
  buy 2321 x40 nearest
  buy 4291 x100 nearest
  buy 17034 x32 nearest
  buy 3372 x41 nearest

step Tailoring 150-200: Auction House
  tip What the Enchanting stretch of this band takes that the Auction House sells: 61 Soul Dust, 1 Golden Rod, 1 Iridescent Pearl and 1 Greater Astral Essence. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold. The Tailoring crafts below use only vendor goods and bolts you already made.
  auction 11083 x61
  auction 11128 x1
  auction 5500 x1
  auction 11082 x1

step Soul Dust and Greater Astral Essence
  tip Soul Dust and the greater essences come from disenchanting greens of item level 21-40. The Crimson Silk Vests, Crimson Silk Pantaloons and Black Mageweave Leggings you craft below are your own supply: disenchant every green one that is not an upgrade for you. Pearls turn up inside clams and a Blacksmith makes the Golden Rod, so the Auction House is the sane way to get those.
  collect 11083 x61 anywhere gather Enchanting 1
  collect 11082 x1 anywhere gather Enchanting 1

step Crimson Silk Vest (150-170)
  tip Crimson Silk Vest, 20 vests to 170: 4 Bolt of Silk Cloth, 2 Red Dye and 2 Fine Thread each. Disenchant the green ones for Soul Dust.
  learn 8791 "Crimson Silk Vest"
  craft 8791 "Crimson Silk Vest" until 170

step Runed Golden Rod (Enchanting 150-151)
  tip Runed Golden Rod, 1 craft to Enchanting 151: 1 Golden Rod, 1 Iridescent Pearl, 1 Greater Astral Essence and 1 Soul Dust. Keep it in your bags: the recipes from 165 need it.
  learn 13628 "Runed Golden Rod"
  craft 13628 "Runed Golden Rod" x1

step Minor Mana Oil (Enchanting 151-165)
  tip Minor Mana Oil, 16 to Enchanting 165: 1 Soul Dust, 2 Maple Seed and 1 Leaded Vial each.
  learn 25125 "Minor Mana Oil"
  craft 25125 "Minor Mana Oil" until 165

step Crimson Silk Pantaloons (170-185)
  tip Crimson Silk Pantaloons, 17 to 185: 4 Bolt of Silk Cloth, 2 Red Dye and 2 Silken Thread each. Disenchant the green ones.
  learn 8799 "Crimson Silk Pantaloons"
  craft 8799 "Crimson Silk Pantaloons" until 185

step Enchant Boots - Lesser Agility (Enchanting 165-200)
  tip Enchant Boots - Lesser Agility, 44 to Enchanting 200: 1 Soul Dust each. Yellow from 180: make a few more if you come up short of 200. Pause for Black Mageweave Leggings whenever the dust runs dry, then come back to this step.
  learn 13637 "Enchant Boots - Lesser Agility"
  craft 13637 "Enchant Boots - Lesser Agility" until 200

step Black Mageweave Leggings (185-200)
  tip Black Mageweave Leggings, 22 to 200: 2 Bolt of Mageweave and 3 Silken Thread each. Yellow the whole way: make a few more if you come up short of 200. These are green: disenchant them, since the dust funds the boots above.
  learn 12049 "Black Mageweave Leggings"
  craft 12049 "Black Mageweave Leggings" until 200

